      "text": "Inkling 2 Mini is a 26-billion-parameter looped mixture-of-experts (MoE) language model developed by Thinking Machines. It uses a recurrent 'looped' architecture where a single set of expert layers is applied iteratively, enabling high parameter efficiency. The model is notable for its deployment via the Project Maya (maya-ik2) engine, which quantizes and batches experts to fit entirely in 24 GB VRAM on an RTX 3090, achieving 128 tokens/second decode with 344K context, image understanding, and tool use. It demonstrates that large MoE models can run locally on consumer hardware without model splitting."
