    "summary": "Thinking Machines' Inkling 2 Mini, a 26B-parameter looped mixture-of-experts model, dominated local-LLM discussions today after a Project Maya port demonstrated 128 token/s decode and 344K context on a single RTX 3090. The maya-inkling-mini GitHub release shows the full model fitting in 24 GB VRAM, with an 8 GB GPU path at 41 token/s, continuous batching, and tool/image support via the maya-ik2 engine. Benchmarks from peaster.io corrected earlier drafter-inflated numbers but confirmed strong prose throughput. Meanwhile, Latent Space's AINews noted Z.ai's new GLM 5.4 looped transformer follows Inkling Mini 2's architecture, and highlighted Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang's surprise return. Other trending terms today include qwen-image-2.1 (Alibaba's latest image generator), cfg (classifier-free guidance in diffusion), turbo (fast LoRA fine-tuning), and chatr (a conversational model).",
